# systemd-homed is not installed or run in this container; only shared libraries are present.
CVE-2026-16742

# This advisory applies to the OpenSSH server (sshd), which is not in openssh-client.
CVE-2026-59999
CVE-2026-60000

# This libxml2 advisory affects its Python bindings; the image does not install
# python3-libxml2 or lxml, so only the unrelated libxml2 C library is present.
CVE-2026-74860

# This libxml2 issue is a denial of service in XML internal-subset parsing.
# Debian classifies it as minor for Trixie; no included service parses untrusted
# XML automatically. Keep the other libxml2 memory-safety findings visible.
CVE-2026-6653

# This ncurses issue is limited to the infocmp command-line utility processing
# untrusted terminfo. The agent image has no service that invokes infocmp, and
# Debian classifies it as a minor issue for Trixie. Reassess if that changes.
CVE-2025-69720

# Archive::Tar can exhaust memory on a crafted tar header, but only when Perl
# code explicitly parses that input. No image service or startup tool does so;
# Debian has postponed the fix while upstream regressions are resolved.
CVE-2026-9538

# This libacl flaw requires a privileged process to perform ACL operations on
# an attacker-controlled symlink path. The agents image runs as the unprivileged
# agent user and has no privileged ACL service.
CVE-2026-54369

# These Go findings affect server-only code paths: SSH server authentication
# callbacks, gRPC xDS server creation, and inbound gRPC HTTP/2 handling. This
# image includes the Argo CD CLI (not argocd-server) and rclone, whose optional
# remote-control endpoint is HTTP; neither starts an SSH or gRPC server.
CVE-2026-56854
CVE-2026-84304
CVE-2026-84445
